Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Canan Uncu
Author-Name: Osman Eroğlu
Author-Workplace-Name: mardin artuklu üniversitesi
Title: Bank Employees and Quıet Quıttıng: an Evaluatıon of Quıet Quıttıng Wıthın the Framework of Burnout Syndrome
Abstract: This study aims to examine the relationship between burnout syndrome and quiet quitting tendencies among employees working in the banking sector. Adopting a quantitative research method, data were collected through a survey from 305 participants employed in public and private banks across Turkey. The Maslach Burnout Inventory and the Quiet Quitting Scale were used in the study, and the obtained data were analyzed using correlation, regression, t-test, and ANOVA analyses. The findings indicate a strong and positive relationship between burnout syndrome and quiet quitting. In particular, the dimensions of emotional exhaustion and reduced personal accomplishment were found to significantly predict all subdimensions of quiet quitting. Additionally, levels of quiet quitting and burnout differed according to age, education level, and length of service, while a significant difference based on institutional status was observed only for quiet quitting. The results reveal that quiet quitting is a behavioral manifestation of burnout and underscore the importance of organizational practices that prioritize employee well-being.
