Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Mohammed Omar
Author-Workplace-Name: University of Zakho
Author-Name: Ismael Mousa
Author-Workplace-Name: Duhok University
Title: Automation of Government Accounting and Its Impact on Operational Efficiency and Transparency
Abstract: This study investigates the impact of accounting automation on financial data accuracy, operational efficiency, cost reduction, and transparency in governmental institutions under the Independent Administration of Zakho. A qualitative approach was employed, using semi-structured interviews with seven participants, including accounting managers and two academic experts. Data were analyzed thematically to extract key insights. Findings reveal that accounting automation improves the speed and accuracy of financial reporting, reduces human errors, and strengthens internal controls, enhancing transparency and accountability. Its effectiveness relies on technological infrastructure, internet stability, and employees’ competencies in modern accounting systems. While implementation requires substantial investment in software, hardware, and training, long-term benefits include improved efficiency, lower administrative costs, and more reliable financial data. The study contributes empirical evidence on digital transformation in governmental accounting and recommends upgrading infrastructure, continuous professional training, cybersecurity enhancement, and systematic data quality monitoring to maximize automation benefits.
